course: dictionary
lesson: 11524
title: Alleyways
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An alleyway is a narrow path or lane that runs between or behind buildings. Context helps you find its meaning. «The cat slipped down the alleyway behind the shops.» A cat slipping down a place behind shops is a clue that an alleyway is a narrow way between buildings.
explain: Stories often use alleyways to create a mood. «The alleyway was dark and quiet, and footsteps echoed off the walls.» Words like dark, quiet and echoed make you feel uneasy, so the writer is building a spooky or secret feeling. The clues tell you how the writer wants you to feel.
explain: In real life, safety matters. «Dad said we must never walk alone down a dark alleyway.» This is a rule, and the word dark tells you why: an empty, dark alleyway can be unsafe. Alleyways can also be useful. «Our short cut to school goes through a narrow alleyway.» Here the alleyway is a quick way to get somewhere.
fact: An alleyway is a narrow path or lane between or behind buildings.
fact: «Alleyway» is a noun. Its plural is «alleyways».
fact: In stories, alleyways are often dark, secret or spooky.
fact: In safety lessons, children are told to avoid dark alleyways when they are alone.
fact: An alleyway can be a short cut through a town.
exercise: «The cat slipped down the alleyway behind the shops.» What is an alleyway? | *A narrow path or lane between or behind buildings | A wide road with lots of cars | A big garden at the front of a house | A large park with a lake
exercise: «Dad said we must never walk alone down a dark alleyway.» Why does Dad give this rule? | *A dark, empty alleyway can be unsafe | Alleyways are always too wide to walk down | Alleyways are full of flowers and sunshine
exercise: «Our short cut to school goes through a narrow alleyway.» What does short cut mean? | A rule you must follow | *A quicker way to get somewhere | A long, slow walk | A road that is closed
test: «The alleyway was dark and quiet, and footsteps echoed off the walls.» What mood does this create? | Loud and busy | *Spooky and secret | Calm and cheerful | Hot and sunny
test: What is the plural of alleyway? | *alleyways | alleyway-s | alleyway's | alleywaies
exam: Why does Dad say never walk alone down a dark alleyway? | *Dark, empty alleyways can be unsafe | Alleyways are too narrow to walk down | Alleyways are always the fastest way to school | Alleyways are where the shops sell sweets
